{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "01a08154-4c27-7551-9cfa-e8e7d2bcf73a", "turn_id": "01a0ed8f-1189-7960-bd49-7cd7b4e89509", "item_id": "exec-9cbd55db-2ba3-4818-9b62-def34ff2f63a", "rollout_ordinal": 758, "created_at_ms": 1790692054073, "item_type": "webSearch", "updated_at_ordinal": 758, "started_at_ms": 1790692054073, "completed_at_ms": 1790692056526}, "item": {"type": "webSearch", "id": "exec-9cbd55db-2ba3-4818-9b62-def34ff2f63a", "query": "github MIR-1K PitchLabel arange 0.02 0.02 midi_to_hz ...", "action": {"type": "search", "query": null, "queries": ["github MIR-1K PitchLabel arange 0.02 0.02 midi_to_hz", "site.mirlab.org MIR-1K pitch labels 20 ms first frame"]}, "results": [{"type": "text_result", "domain": "github.com", "ref_id": "turn8search0", "snippet": "# Make sure frequency values are 1-d np ndarrays ... \"\"\"Convert Hz to MIDI numbers ... \"\"\"Convert MIDI numbers to Hz ... f\"{func.__module__}.{func.__name__}\\n\\tDeprecated as of", "title": "mir_eval/mir_eval/util.py at main · mir-evaluation/mir_eval · GitHub", "url": "https://github.com/mir-evaluation/mir_eval/blob/main/mir_eval/util.py"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "github.com", "ref_id": "turn8search1", "snippet": "# mir1k.py ... [Input: Go to file] ... # mir1k.py ... def midi2hz(midi): ... pitch_folder = \"PitchLabel\"", "title": "pytorch-wav-datasets/mir1k.py at master · yoyolicoris/pytorch-wav-datasets · GitHub", "url": "https://github.com/yoyolicoris/pytorch-wav-datasets/blob/master/mir1k.py"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "github.com", "ref_id": "turn8search2", "snippet": "Download the dataset from here and place it under `$DATA_DIR/MIR-1K/` with the following structure: ... ├── PitchLabel └── Wavfile ... Convert the F0 annotations from", "title": "f0-mlf/README.md at main · groupmm/f0-mlf · GitHub", "url": "https://github.com/groupmm/f0-mlf/blob/main/README.md"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "transactions.ismir.net", "ref_id": "turn8search12", "snippet": "reconstructs the input frame using a decoder and ... annotations are provided with a hop size of 20 ms forMIR-1K, 2.904 ms (128/44100) for MDB-stem-synth,", "title": "PESTO: Real-Time Pitch", "url": "https://transactions.ismir.net/articles/251/files/68c0346a4b785.pdf"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "github.com", "ref_id": "turn8search3", "snippet": "The project uses the MIR-1K dataset, which contains: * 1000+ singing voice segments from Chinese karaoke recordings ... │ ├── Wavfile/ │ ├── PitchLabel/ ...", "title": "GitHub - linhnv04/vocal_pitch_detection · GitHub", "url": "https://github.com/linhnv04/vocal_pitch_detection"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "zenodo.org", "ref_id": "turn8search13", "snippet": "Raw Pitch Accuracy obtained by SWIPE implementations on the MIR-1K and MDB-stem-synth datasets, compared to baseline values previously reported in self-supervised pitch estimation papers. ...", "title": "Proceedings of the 26th ISMIR Conference, Daejeon, Korea, September 21-25, 2025", "url": "https://zenodo.org/record/17706561/files/000080.pdf"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "music-ir.org", "ref_id": "turn8search4", "snippet": "* The first window is centered in 20ms (the window size is 40ms and the overlap is 20ms). ... Or maybe a dummy pitch value", "title": "2009:Audio Melody Extraction - MIREX Wiki", "url": "https://music-ir.org/mirex/wiki/2009%3AAudio_Melody_Extraction"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "citeseerx.ist.psu.edu", "ref_id": "turn8search14", "snippet": "information was calculated using linear interpolation from the original 20ms frame pitch ... algorithm to discriminate voiced/unvoiced frames could be to label everything as voiced", "title": "Study of reverberation robust pitch estimators", "url": "https://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/document?doi=cd8a567af97b3207c46ce7936304b9f77149f694&repid=rep1&type=pdf"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "gist.github.com", "ref_id": "turn8search5", "snippet": "| \"\"\"Round the given pitch values to the nearest MIDI note numbers\"\"\" | midi_note = np.around(librosa.hz_to_midi(f0)) ... | for i in np.arange(f0.shape[0]): ... | def", "title": "Autotune stereo recording of a solo instrument · GitHub", "url": "https://gist.github.com/liebharc/b8f97f82eae22f49573330cd227589a2"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "code.soundsoftware.ac.uk", "ref_id": "turn8search15", "snippet": "duration in MIR-1k dataset. ... provides the label of “unvoiced frame”, so we can train our model ... Score pitch: The first concern is that", "title": "ON THE PREPARATION AND VALIDATION OF A LARGE-SCALE DATASET", "url": "https://code.soundsoftware.ac.uk/attachments/download/2806/ON%20THE%20PREPARATION%20AND%20VALIDATION%20OF%20A%20LARGE-SCALE%20DATASET%20OF%20SINGING%20TRANSCRIPTION.pdf"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "github.com", "ref_id": "turn8search6", "snippet": "## File metadata and controls ... Signal Processing, 2007(1):154-163, Jan. ... frequency_index = np.arange(0, n_times) ... # convert frequencies from Hz to continuous midi note", "title": "mir_eval/mir_eval/multipitch.py at main · mir-evaluation/mir_eval · GitHub", "url": "https://github.com/mir-evaluation/mir_eval/blob/main/mir_eval/multipitch.py"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "music-and-culture-technology-lab.github.io", "ref_id": "turn8search7", "snippet": "class omnizart.constants.datasets.MIR1KStructure¶ ... test_labels = ['PitchLabel']¶", "title": "Constants", "url": "https://music-and-culture-technology-lab.github.io/omnizart-doc/constants.html"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "gist.github.com", "ref_id": "turn8search8", "snippet": "| from mir_eval.melody import hz2cents ... | cents = np.array([self.labeling.f0_label2c(contours[i + start_idx, :], path[i]) for i in range(len(path))]) ... | time_idx = np.arange(len(path)) + start_i", "title": "violin2midi.py · GitHub", "url": "https://gist.github.com/dummyjenil/40ee550e0f6097fb6e669aefc10ec584"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "github.com", "ref_id": "turn8search9", "snippet": ".github | .github | | ... > Chroma, chord and key detection moved to @audio/mir (`mir-chroma`, `mir-chord`, `mir-key`). ... > Works in Node.js and browser.", "title": "GitHub - audiojs/pitch: Pitch detection algorithms · GitHub", "url": "https://github.com/audiojs/pitch"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "nanless.github.io", "ref_id": "turn8search10", "snippet": "收益是参数少 35.9% 而精度不掉：MDB 上低秩 99.07 对基线 98.98，高 0.09 点，种子标准差仅 0.010，配对 t 达 18.8，真实但可忽略；PTDB 差 -0.13 点，种子标准差 0.234，配对 t 为 -0.50 且 3 种子符号不一致，不可区分；MIR-1K 差 +0.02", "title": "Low-Rank Frequency Convolution and Noise-Range Augmentation for Real-Time Pitch Estimation on Edge Devices | 语音/音乐/音频论文速递", "url": "https://nanless.github.io/audio-paper-digest-blog/posts/2026-09-22-low-rank-frequency-convolution-and-noise-range-2609-23340/"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "gist.github.com", "ref_id": "turn8search11", "snippet": "| plt.title(\"F0 Contour for \" + audio_file + \" extracted with Parselmouth\") ... | frequency = librosa.midi_to_hz(note.pitch) ... | label = \"MIDI F0 (low-pass)\" if", "title": "f0_contour_experiment.py · GitHub", "url": "https://gist.github.com/john-d-murphy/ae743b67bcd8942a5792500c91f8d98c"}]}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "01a08154-4c27-7551-9cfa-e8e7d2bcf73a", "turn_id": "01a0ed8f-1189-7960-bd49-7cd7b4e89509", "item_id": "rs_06f6aa8593d2a892016abbcadbbf7487d2b775ee46558b9966", "rollout_ordinal": 761, "created_at_ms": 1790692059984, "item_type": "reasoning", "updated_at_ordinal": 761, "started_at_ms": 1790692059984, "completed_at_ms": 1790692067767}, "item": {"type": "reasoning", "id": "rs_06f6aa8593d2a892016abbcadbbf7487d2b775ee46558b9966", "summary": [], "content": []}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "01a08154-4c27-7551-9cfa-e8e7d2bcf73a", "turn_id": "01a0ed8f-1189-7960-bd49-7cd7b4e89509", "item_id": "msg_06f6aa8593d2a892016abbcae3969487d2a84c050be6c18dcb", "rollout_ordinal": 763, "created_at_ms": 1790692067805, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 763, "started_at_ms": 1790692067805, "completed_at_ms": 1790692070123}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "msg_06f6aa8593d2a892016abbcae3969487d2a84c050be6c18dcb", "text": "El servidor original de MIR-1K no responde. Encontré una copia pública con los audios y las etiquetas separados. Haré una primera prueba con cinco fragmentos por cantante, seleccionados de forma reproducible, y registraré exactamente cuáles se usaron. Así podremos comparar voz sola y voz con música sin volver a ajustar el detector.\n", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
